Exact N=4 quotient channels for extendability
==============================================================================
{'channel': 'edge_count', 'groups': 3, 'mixed_extendability_buckets': 0, 'max_bucket': 12}
{'channel': 'degree_histogram', 'groups': 3, 'mixed_extendability_buckets': 0, 'max_bucket': 12}
{'channel': 'rooted_first3_degrees', 'groups': 8, 'mixed_extendability_buckets': 0, 'max_bucket': 3}
{'channel': 'full_coloring', 'groups': 18, 'mixed_extendability_buckets': 0, 'max_bucket': 1}
For this tiny pair case, even edge_count separates extendability.  The lesson is not that scalars always work; it is that the next useful coordinate is a derivative one: how many bad children remain.

